\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262969 1113 #uuid "9cc31f35-4916-5f32-a8c9-fe9e2d10f162" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262969 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2t}{3{t}^{2}+4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3t+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=2,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2} & =\\frac{2}{3(2)+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262971 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262972 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1041 "field-1" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262972 13194139533878 true] [17592186262970 1110 #uuid "2ef2b9f2-2901-50b6-91bc-9e88c0f87ff0" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262971 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262971 1111 #uuid "959affd4-d5f0-5fff-b1d2-e6f856077e47" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262972 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262972 1111 #uuid "d7c0bed7-a207-5331-8131-6ff7423443b9" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262974 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1089 "q-353341" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949328/assets/1817c65aea37112d93f2935801a0e7dcd654706a72f729810272f48e95d39665.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /6}=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1113 #uuid "6f44a7e1-514a-5573-bc6d-02d50696e90b" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262973 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262975 13194139533878 true] [17592186262974 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533878 true] [17592186262974 1041 "field-1" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262974 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262975 13194139533878 true] [17592186262974 1110 #uuid "8ce3f65f-2ff0-5ad3-9dd8-0d12e0552286" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262975 1034 "-\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262975 1111 #uuid "fc1b76fb-62f5-5fe4-970b-d337f5125634" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262977 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1089 "q-6816" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{2t},\\,y=({t}^{2}-1){e}^{-t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1113 #uuid "1990413b-418b-52e9-8b02-51eb17f5b4b1" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262976 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}}{2{e}^{2t}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2(1)-(1)^{2}){e}^{-3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2-1){e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262978 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262979 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262980 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262981 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262982 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1041 "selection" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262981 13194139533878 true] [17592186262977 1110 #uuid "7624c062-786d-5f09-942a-66bf33c08d66" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262978 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{-3}}{4}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262978 1111 #uuid "edefa64c-fcbd-59cb-9d3c-9be1fbec8796" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262979 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262979 1111 #uuid "5d8106ae-4c2f-5db9-977f-aeb769344f5e" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262980 1034 "{e}^{-2}" 13194139533878 true] [17592186262980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533878 true] [17592186262980 1111 #uuid "a65fc94c-0deb-